  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5004.03 Application Procedures. Any person who wishes to apply for an original license to store display fireworks shall:\n\n(a) Be 21 years of age or older, in accordance with RSA 160-B;\n\n(b) Appear in person at the New Hampshire department of safety during normal business hours;\n\n(c) Supply proof of identification such as a valid driver’s license or birth certificate;\n\n(d) Complete and submit the application, form DSSP 110, “Application for License to Use, Purchase and Transport Explosives”, revised 05/13;\n\n(e) Shall provide a copy of a valid U.S. ATF&E license for the storage of Display Fireworks, or explosives;\n\n(f) Make payment of the fee as specified in RSA 158:9-c; and\n\n(g) Provide written approval to store fireworks from the local fire chief that has jurisdiction for the storage site.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; amd by #7481, eff 4-25-01; paragraphs (a)(1)-(5) and (b) EXPIRED: 7-1-03; amd by #8117, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04; paragraphs (a)(1)-(5) and (b) EXPIRED: 1-10-05; amd by #8261, eff 1-21-05; ss by #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12124, eff 3-6-17; ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
